WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.640
Guides: staying with your guard all day, and tapping each step as it happens.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:19.390
On contest day, opening your family page takes you straight to your station screen. If your coordinator assigned you a guard, it opens right on them: their performance time, warm-up area, and home room.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.873
The big button is your next step, with the time it's scheduled for. Tap it when it actually happens.

00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:31.400
Above it: where your guard's props are, and whether their equipment is through inspection.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:40.560
Every tap asks first, so a pocket tap doesn't count. Forgot to tap a step before? Leave the box checked and it's marked too.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:50.910
Things happen out of order, and that's OK. Nothing is ever blocked. If inspection isn't done yet, it just tells you, and HQ sees a flag.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.502
All your steps are listed below, with the scheduled times. Tapped one by mistake? Tap it again to take it back.

00:00:58.702 --> 00:01:05.188
After the performance and tarp folding, Transit back to HR also tells the prop crew to head to loading.

00:01:05.388 --> 00:01:10.690
Once everything is out, HR cleared gives the home room back for a later guard.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:18.970
No guard assigned yet? When yours checks in, tap Claim. One guide per guard, and everyone else sees it's yours.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:24.322
Have to leave? Hand off, and tell your coordinator, so someone picks up your guard.

00:01:24.522 --> 00:01:30.360
Questions? Call or text your coordinator. They handle anything that needs a director.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:37.640
Thanks for guiding. Stay with your guard, tap as it happens, and clear the home room before you go.
